  "findings": [
    "odg-agent-supervisor repo-evidence mode approximates an unowned live worktree's write-set from git-observed paths (branch diff / dirty); gitignored runtime/generated writes of its live processes are invisible, and with no observed path it is UNKNOWN => every assign refused. Outcome therefore depends on git state, not on what the processes write. Not changed (design trade-off; owner decision).",
    "renew(status CANCELLED) refreshes heartbeatAt, so a dead agent looks RUNNING for staleMs and close() is refused until it goes stale (measured: closeRightAfterCancel REFUSED (state RUNNING), CLOSED_REJECTED after staleMs). Not changed.",
    "decideRecovery never RELAUNCHes a wave child (no worktree => NOT_RECOVERABLE); recovery of a wave child goes through the tick's ledger dedup, and the supervisor's work-item dedup requires cancel+close of the interrupted heartbeat first.",
    "a SIGKILL that lands after the ledger stage leaves a PROVEN ledger entry while the attempt log says FAIL; the next tick dedups it (no re-run, no duplicate). The harness only counts a kill as an interruption when the child had no report and no ledger entry (killedLedgerAfterTick1 = 0).",
    "a dead ledger-claim holder blocks recording until the 120 s TTL (within-TTL tick fails closed after the 60 s claim timeout); reclaim at TTL is correct (re-measured here, same as #896).",
    "odg-run has no in-process heartbeat and the tick is not wired to the supervisor: supervision of wave children is harness-bridged."
